@startuml
title Proposed security trust boundaries — complete product
actor User
cloud "Untrusted public network" as Network
package "User-controlled device boundary" {
 [Web / Android / iOS Client] as Client
}
package "Controlled service boundary (provider TBD)" {
 [Authenticated API] as API
 [Authorization and domain services] as Domain
 [Identity boundary] as IdP
 [Audit / outbox] as Audit
}
database "Private transactional data" as DB
folder "Private receipt objects" as Blob
cloud "Notification provider" as Notify
User --> Client
Client --> Network
Network --> API : TLS; bearer/session credential
API --> IdP : verify identity
API --> Domain
Domain --> DB : least-privilege access
Domain --> Blob : scoped receipt access
Domain --> Audit
Audit --> Notify : post-commit dispatch
note right of Domain
Authorize every group-scoped read/write
using current server-side membership.
Client checks alone are insufficient.
end note
@enduml
